 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Totally normal. The key is confidence. Order your food as it were already on plate, and pay for it. Then you're a guest rather than someone waiting for food. Not necessarily, but bring it up front so you have it. Sit at a neat spot so everyone can see you. And remember, you're there to enjoy food, not host it. Love it. The broth is always cold, though, so ask for it hot and add extra soup ramen at start. That's nice. Order something with a big piece of pasta or pastries for dessert. People always end up taking small bites of it.",
